#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f51eeb-87d3-5f06-9404-e21666f85c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20f51eeb-87d3-5f06-9404-e21666f85c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329601} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6dc0cac-3e51-5c86-afe9-d37ced4615bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "46a75f72-6b10-51d9-969a-5bb2a80a1f23" :question/math-academy-id "q-280321" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,-3,2),$ $B(4,-1,5),$ $C(-2,0,1),$ and $D(3,-2,3).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i-j+5k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j+3k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1)-2((-3)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3((-3)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(3+1)-2(-3+2)+3(-3-6) \\\\  & =12+2-27 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-13|=13.\n$$"}]}
